Grand Junction Aviation Discussion

Issued at 0019 UTC Sunday, August 10, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 614 PM MDT Sat Aug 9 2025

Wind gusts 25 to 35 mph will continue through early evening

before dropping off after sunset and becoming lighter and

terrain driven. North to northwest winds will push wildfire

smoke back over KASE, KRIL and KGJT this evening and overnight

into Sunday morning before mixing Sunday afternoon helps improve

visibility some. Although KASE, KRIL and KGJT are the more

likely sites to experience reduced visibilities due to wildfire

smoke. Otherwise, VFR conditions should prevail. Winds Sunday

afternoon are not expected to be as strong but still gusting 20

to 30 mph at times.





