Salt Lake City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2009 UTC Saturday, August  9, 2025



.AVIATION...KSLC...VFR conditions to prevail at the KSLC terminal

through the period. Winds remain generally light out of the 

northwest through around 04-05z before transitioning 

southeasterly. A mid-to-high level cloud deck brings scattered to 

broken sky coverage into Sunday morning.

.REST OF UTAH AND SOUTHWEST WYOMING...VFR conditions to prevail 

at all regional terminals through the TAF period. Scattered to 

broken mid-to-high level cloud coverage is expected across the 

northern half of the airspace this afternoon and evening, then 

across the southern portion of the airspace this evening into 

early Sunday morning. Winds remain generally light areawide, 

though some elevated west-northwest breezes are possible across 

southern Utah terminals this afternoon.





