Goodland Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2134 UTC Saturday, August  9, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SUNDAY/... 

Issued at 328 PM MDT Sat Aug 9 2025

Main focus for this TAF period will be increasing shower and

storm activity. Confidence in severe impacts for each terminal 

is low due to the splitting nature of the storms so will 

continue with the PROB30. Better potential for rainfall is 

overnight however. Winds are forecast to be shifting quite a bit

with any outflow boundaries as well. Rain chance look to end 

Sunday morning before another potential round moves in just 

after this TAF period primarily for GLD. 



Dodge City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2326 UTC Saturday, August  9, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 622 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025

A cluster of scattered Supercell thunderstorms over northeast

Colorado are forecast to congeal into more of an organized line

of storms or larger clusters by mid to late evening over 

northwest Kansas. It is during this period after about 02z and 

through about 08z where our best chances for thunderstorms with 

local MVFR/IFR cigs and vsby impacting the local terminals. A 

localized mile and a half in 2000ft CB at any of the sw KS 

terminals for a sub 1 hour period, and possible more than one 

instance as the scattered thunderstorms the HRRR brings them

across the area. That said, the northern terminals GCK/HYS/DDC,

have a better chance for storms impacts (20-40% based on HREF 

marginal MVFR probabilities) than say, LBL farther south. A 

prolific gusty westerly surface flow should develop everywhere.





