Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2340 UTC Saturday, August  9, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 526 PM MDT Sat Aug 9 2025

Weak showers and thunderstorms across the Southwest and South 

Central Mountains will persist through 02Z or so. Additional

shower and thunderstorm development remains possible across

eastern NM this evening through 04Z. If this activity develops, a

few storms may produce gusty and erratic winds in excess of 40kt,

and across far northeast NM, some hail as well. Thereafter, quiet

conditions are expected overnight, except LLWS at KTCC once again.

A cold front/outflow boundary will push into NE NM around 08-09Z

before continuing to press southward through mid day Sunday. Winds

will switch around to the north with a few breezes. Moisture

behind the boundary will allow for greater coverage of storms on

Sunday, particularly along and east of the Central Mountain Chain.

A few severe storms may develop across northeast NM Sunday

afternoon with large hail and damaging wind gusts. Showers and

thunderstorms with little rainfall and gusty winds will still

prevail across the Southwest Mountains toward the Rio Grande 

Valley. 



