Recreation Forecast

National Weather Service Grand Forks ND

800 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025



Here are the Recreation Area Forecasts...



Wave height forecasts represent the average of the highest 33% of

waves that occur in a given period. Since the significant wave

height is an average of the largest waves, mariners should be

aware that many individual waves will be higher. 



For Devils Lake...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Windy. West winds 10 to 20 mph increasing to

20 to 30 mph after midnight. Waves 1 to 3 feet. Chance of showers

and slight chance of thunderstorms in the evening. Mostly cloudy.

Lows in the upper 50s. 

.SUNDAY...Breezy. West winds 15 to 25 mph. Waves 1 to 3 feet.

Areas of smoke in the late morning and afternoon. Mostly cloudy

in the morning then clearing. Highs in the 70s. 

.SUNDAY NIGHT...Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 2 to 4 feet.

Areas of smoke. Mostly clear. Lows around 60. 





For the Upper and Lower Red Lakes...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Southwest winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 2 to

4 feet. Showers likely and slight chance of thunderstorms in the

evening. Mostly cloudy in the evening then becoming partly

cloudy. Lows in the lower 60s. 

.SUNDAY...West winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 2 to 4 feet subsiding to

1 to 2 feet in the afternoon. Areas of smoke late in the

afternoon. Partly sunny. Highs 65 to 75. 

.SUNDAY NIGHT...Southwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 to 2 feet.

Areas of smoke. Mostly clear. Lows in the lower 60s. 





For Lake of the Woods...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Breezy. Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph

increasing to 15 to 25 mph after midnight. Waves 1 foot or less

building to 3 to 5 feet after midnight. Showers and slight chance

of thunderstorms. Mostly cloudy in the evening then becoming

partly cloudy. Lows around 60. 

.SUNDAY...West winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 3 to 5 feet. Areas of

smoke late in the afternoon. Partly sunny. Highs 65 to 75. 

.SUNDAY NIGHT...Southwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 to 2 feet.

Areas of smoke. Mostly clear. Lows in the lower 60s. 





